  "not_checked": [
    "Full texts. Every study was read from its abstract, and some sample sizes are missing (Awad 2020, Kneer & Christen 2024, Tolmeijer 2022, Franklin 2021).",
    "Forward-citation searches. OpenAlex's free daily budget ran out mid-run and Semantic Scholar rate-limited, so the scouts searched mostly through Crossref. \"No designer-choice experiment found\" is a limited search, not proof of absence; such work may sit in law, HCI or product-liability research under other terms.",
    "Carro & Lagnado 2026 (arXiv 2603.13236), found by the challenger: not read beyond its summary.",
    "The trend counts come from one index, Europe PMC, which leans biomedical. That is why moral injury and distress, common in nursing research, is the largest topic. The same counts were not repeated in OpenAlex.",
    "Phrase sets were not validated by reading samples. \"Robot\" and \"algorithm\" are broad, and \"mind perception\" sits in the moral status topic and overlaps with AI.",
    "\"Moral crumple zone\" was coined (Elish) for humans absorbing blame for automated systems; Hohenstein & Jung use it for the AI absorbing blame. From general knowledge, unverified.",
    "The 2025 jump in all moral records (2,620 to 3,450) may partly be an indexing change.",
    "The experiment's power numbers are rough and its effect sizes are guesses, not from the sources.",
